705	
706	  .two-col {{ display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; }}
707	  @media (max-width: 800px) {{ .two-col {{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; }} }}
708	</style>
709	</head>
710	<body>
711	<div class="report-container">
712	
713	<!-- HEADER -->
714	<div class="report-header">
715	  <h1>Amazon Product Catalog Performance &amp; Customer Sentiment Analysis</h1>
716	  <div class="subtitle">A comprehensive analysis of {total_products:,} Amazon India products examining pricing strategies, discount effectiveness, customer ratings, and category-level performance.</div>
717	  <div class="meta">Dataset: Amazon India Catalog &bull; Products Analyzed: {total_products:,} &bull; Report Date: April 2026</div>
718	</div>
719	
720	<!-- SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW -->
721	<div class="section" id="executive-overview">
722	  <h2 class="section-title">Executive Overview</h2>
723	  <p class="section-desc">Headline KPIs providing a snapshot of catalog health, promotional intensity, and customer engagement.</p>
724	
725	  <div class="kpi-grid">
726	    <div class="kpi-card">
727	      <div class="kpi-value">{total_products:,}</div>
728	      <div class="kpi-label">Products Analyzed</div>
729	    </div>
730	    <div class="kpi-card">
731	      <div class="kpi-value green">{avg_rating:.2f}</div>
732	      <div class="kpi-label">Average Product Rating</div>
733	    </div>
734	    <div class="kpi-card">
735	      <div class="kpi-value orange">{avg_discount:.1f}%</div>
736	      <div class="kpi-label">Average Discount Percentage</div>
737	    </div>
738	    <div class="kpi-card">
739	      <div class="kpi-value">{median_rating_count:,.0f}</div>
740	      <div class="kpi-label">Median Rating Count</div>
741	    </div>
742	    <div class="kpi-card">
743	      <div class="kpi-value green">{high_rating_share:.1f}%</div>
744	      <div class="kpi-label">Products Rated 4.0+</div>
745	    </div>
746	    <div class="kpi-card">
747	      <div class="kpi-value">{corr_discount_rating:+.3f}</div>
748	      <div class="kpi-label">Discount-Rating Correlation</div>
749	    </div>
750	  </div>
751	
752	  <div class="insight-box">
753	    <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> The catalog shows strong overall quality — <strong>{high_rating_share:.1f}%</strong> of products maintain a 4.0+ rating. The average discount of <strong>{avg_discount:.1f}%</strong> is substantial, yet the near-zero correlation ({corr_discount_rating:+.3f}) between discounts and ratings indicates that deeper discounts do not meaningfully improve customer satisfaction.
754	  </div>
755	</div>
756	
757	<!-- SECTION 2: CATEGORY PERFORMANCE -->
758	<div class="section" id="category-analysis">
759	  <h2 class="section-title">Category Performance Breakdown</h2>
760	  <p class="section-desc">How products are distributed across top-level categories, and which segments lead or lag in ratings and engagement.</p>
761	
762	  <div class="chart-row">
763	    <div class="chart-container">{chart_cat_distribution}</div>
764	    <div class="chart-container">{chart_cat_donut}</div>
765	  </div>
766	
767	  <div class="card">
768	    <h3>Rating vs. Discount by Category</h3>
769	    {chart_cat_grouped}
770	  </div>
771	
772	  <div class="two-col">
773	    <div class="card">
774	      <h3>Top 5 Categories by Rating</h3>
775	      {table_html(best_cats.rename(columns={{'top_category':'Category','avg_rating':'Avg Rating','count':'Products','avg_discount':'Avg Discount %','median_reviews':'Median Reviews'}}))}
776	    </div>
777	    <div class="card">
778	      <h3>Bottom 5 Categories by Rating (min 5 products)</h3>
779	      {table_html(worst_cats.rename(columns={{'top_category':'Category','avg_rating':'Avg Rating','count':'Products','avg_discount':'Avg Discount %','median_reviews':'Median Reviews'}}))}
780	    </div>
781	  </div>
782	
783	  <div class="card">
784	    <h3>Average Rating by Category</h3>
785	    {chart_cat_rating}
786	  </div>
787	
788	  <div class="insight-box success">
789	    <strong>Insight:</strong> {best_cats.iloc[0]['top_category']} leads with an average rating of <strong>{best_cats.iloc[0]['avg_rating']:.2f}</strong>, while {worst_cats.iloc[0]['top_category']} trails at <strong>{worst_cats.iloc[0]['avg_rating']:.2f}</strong>. Categories with the highest product counts don't always deliver the best satisfaction — volume does not equal quality.
790	  </div>
791	</div>
792	
793	<!-- SECTION 3: PRICING & DISCOUNT STRATEGY -->
794	<div class="section" id="pricing-discount-analysis">
795	  <h2 class="section-title">Pricing &amp; Discount Strategy Analysis</h2>
796	  <p class="section-desc">Examining whether deeper discounts correlate with higher customer satisfaction or merely drive review volume.</p>
797	
798	  <div class="card">
799	    <h3>Discount vs. Rating — Scatter Analysis</h3>
800	    {chart_scatter_discount_rating}
801	    <div class="insight-box" style="margin-top:16px;">
802	      <strong>Correlation Analysis:</strong> Discount % vs. Rating shows a Pearson correlation of <strong>{corr_discount_rating:+.3f}</strong> — a negligible relationship. Discount % vs. Review Count shows r = <strong>{corr_discount_reviews:+.3f}</strong>. Discounts are {'weakly associated with higher review volume' if corr_discount_reviews > 0.05 else 'not meaningfully associated with review volume either'}.
803	    </div>
804	  </div>
805	
806	  <div class="chart-row">
807	    <div class="chart-container">{chart_discount_buckets}</div>
808	    <div class="chart-container">{chart_discount_volume}</div>
809	  </div>
810	
811	  <div class="card">
812	    <h3>Discount Bucket Breakdown</h3>
813	    {table_html(bucket_stats.rename(columns={{'discount_bucket':'Discount Range','count':'Products','avg_rating':'Avg Rating','median_reviews':'Median Reviews','avg_price':'Avg Discounted Price (₹)'}}))}
814	  </div>
815	
816	  <div class="card">
817	    <h3>Performance by Price Segment</h3>
818	    {chart_price_seg}
819	    <div style="margin-top:16px;">
820	    {table_html(price_seg_stats.rename(columns={{'price_segment':'Price Segment','count':'Products','avg_rating':'Avg Rating','avg_discount':'Avg Discount %','median_reviews':'Median Reviews'}}))}
821	    </div>
822	  </div>
823	
824	  <div class="insight-box warning">
825	    <strong>Key Finding:</strong> Products in the <strong>{best_price_seg['price_segment']}</strong> segment achieve the highest average rating ({best_price_seg['avg_rating']:.2f}), suggesting that customer satisfaction is more closely tied to product quality and price positioning than to promotional discounting. The heaviest-discounted products (80-100%) average {bucket_stats[bucket_stats['discount_bucket']=='80-100%']['avg_rating'].values[0]:.2f} in ratings — {'comparable to' if abs(bucket_stats[bucket_stats['discount_bucket']=='80-100%']['avg_rating'].values[0] - avg_rating) < 0.15 else 'different from'} the catalog average of {avg_rating:.2f}.
826	  </div>
827	</div>
828	
829	<!-- SECTION 4: CUSTOMER ENGAGEMENT & RATING DISTRIBUTION -->
830	<div class="section" id="customer-engagement">
831	  <h2 class="section-title">Customer Engagement &amp; Rating Distribution</h2>
832	  <p class="section-desc">Profiling the distribution of ratings and review volumes across the catalog.</p>
833	
834	  <div class="chart-row">
835	    <div class="chart-container">{chart_rating_hist}</div>
836	    <div class="chart-container">{chart_reviews_hist}</div>
837	  </div>
838	
839	  <div class="card">
840	    <h3>Top 10 Most-Reviewed Products</h3>
841	    {table_html(top_engaged.rename(columns={{'product_name':'Product','top_category':'Category','rating_n':'Rating','rating_count_n':'Reviews','discount_pct_n':'Discount %','discounted_price_n':'Price (₹)'}}).reset_index(drop=True), classes="compact")}
842	  </div>
843	
844	  <div class="insight-box success">
845	    <strong>Insight:</strong> The most-engaged products tend to be in accessible price points (under ₹{top_engaged['discounted_price_n'].median():,.0f}) with moderate to high discounts. High engagement doesn't require premium pricing — it requires the right combination of value, visibility, and product-market fit.
846	  </div>
847	</div>
848	
849	<!-- SECTION 5: REVIEW SENTIMENT SNAPSHOT -->
850	<div class="section" id="review-sentiment-snapshot">
851	  <h2 class="section-title">Review Sentiment Snapshot</h2>
852	  <p class="section-desc">High-level qualitative overview of recurring themes in customer review titles and content.</p>
853	
854	  <div class="chart-row">
855	    <div class="chart-container">{chart_pos_sentiment}</div>
856	    <div class="chart-container">{chart_neg_sentiment}</div>
857	  </div>
858	
859	  <div class="two-col">
860	    <div class="insight-box success">
861	      <strong>Positive Themes:</strong> Customers most frequently praise products as "<strong>{top_positive[0][0]}</strong>" ({top_positive[0][1]:,} mentions), "<strong>{top_positive[1][0]}</strong>" ({top_positive[1][1]:,}), and "<strong>{top_positive[2][0]}</strong>" ({top_positive[2][1]:,}). Satisfaction drivers center on perceived value, quality, and performance meeting expectations.
862	    </div>
863	    <div class="insight-box warning">
864	      <strong>Negative Themes:</strong> The most common complaints involve "<strong>{top_negative[0][0]}</strong>" ({top_negative[0][1]:,} mentions), "<strong>{top_negative[1][0]}</strong>" ({top_negative[1][1]:,}), and "<strong>{top_negative[2][0]}</strong>" ({top_negative[2][1]:,}). These point to quality inconsistency and durability concerns as the primary dissatisfaction drivers.
865	    </div>
866	  </div>
867	</div>
868	
869	<!-- SECTION 6: STRATEGIC RECOMMENDATIONS -->
870	<div class="section" id="recommendations">
871	  <h2 class="section-title">Strategic Recommendations</h2>
872	  <p class="section-desc">Actionable recommendations synthesized directly from the data analysis above.</p>
873	
874	  <div class="card">
875	    <ol class="rec-list">
876	      <li>
877	        <strong>Shift from Deep Discounting to Value Positioning</strong>
878	        The near-zero correlation (r = {corr_discount_rating:+.3f}) between discount depth and customer ratings proves that slashing prices doesn't improve satisfaction. Instead, focus on communicating product quality and value at moderate discount levels (40-60% range shows the strongest rating performance at {rec1_val}).
879	        <div class="data-point">Supporting data: Discount-Rating correlation = {corr_discount_rating:+.3f}; 40-60% discount bucket avg rating = {rec1_val}</div>
880	      </li>
881	      <li>
